+
+Parent released ONE diagnostics-only absent-follower run, not a clock repair.
+Data shape: optional fixture-owned diagnostic metadata on the existing Clock:
+election/write/drain phase, issued/applied/last protocol progress, host elapsed
+of the last real Applied receipt, and aggregate total/gated poll counts. Reuse
+existing node dump plus authoritative persistence/snapshot/connector usage.
+Emit only election/quarter/drain receipts and the existing hang failure; no
+per-poll logging, new public/library seam or duplicate job ownership tracking.
+
+Transitions: only actual Applied outcomes update last real host progress.
+Accepted offers update issued metadata before polling; entry to shutdown marks
+drain. Counters observe the EXISTING native-pending predicate without changing
+its evaluation, clock admission, polling/yields, timeouts or work admission.
+Failure output includes host age since the last real Applied receipt, distinguishing
+slow continuing work from a stuck predicate if the unchanged bound fires.
+Metadata owns no sockets/jobs/credits/threads; existing stop/drain/worker joins,
+restart/partial-progress semantics and reclaim paths stay unchanged.
